      "contentHash": "0b291a73486e57001497b0a2c627d100021b8ff15180c3681742ecb2ddee66a6",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: Consolidate every SideStage plan into the SideStage project and make History complete\nslug: sidestage-plan-harness-migration-history-completeness-2026-08-14\nstatus: ready\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n## Goal\n\nMake the `sidestage` harness the single canonical project scope for every SideStage implementation, acceptance, release, and SideStage-created shared-library plan, then make the app History page render that complete ledger.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Preserve plan slugs, contents, statuses, revisions, decisions, item state, and linked work-item evidence.\n- Snapshot the datastore before migration and migrate transactionally.\n- Resolve any slug conflict explicitly; never overwrite a destination plan.\n- History must export the complete sidestage harness, not infer membership from a slug prefix.\n- Verify focused tests, build/type checks, and the running History page with Verdict.\n\n\n## Phase — Migration and verification\n\n- **P-001** `done` Freeze the exact source/destination inventory, classify shared-library plans, and prove there are no slug conflicts. importance: high — note: ← WI-39107 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Create a pre-destructive backup and transactionally migrate every out-of-scope SideStage plan plus dependent plan/work-item references into the sidestage harness. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39108 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `todo` Change the History generator and summary logic so the complete sidestage harness is exported and shipped plans are terminal; add focused regression tests. blocked-by: P-002 importance: high\n- **P-004** `todo` Regenerate the committed History snapshot and run focused API/web tests plus type/build checks. blocked-by: P-003 importance: high\n- **P-005** `todo` Browser-verify All time completeness, migrated/shared plans, statuses, popup documents, and console/network health. blocked-by: P-004 importance: high\n\n\n\n\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D-001 — The dedicated SideStage harness is canonical\nDate: 2026-08-14\nAll plan records whose product scope is SideStage, including acceptance/release plans and shared-library work created as part of SideStage, belong to the `sidestage` harness. The History export selects that harness as the authority and does not impose a slug-prefix filter.\n\n### D-002 — The generalized Project History pipeline remains in the Papercusp harness\nDate: 2026-08-15\n`generalized-project-history-pipeline-2026-08-14` was created after the 38-plan inventory froze. It mentions SideStage because SideStage is its first consumer, but its scope and D-002 explicitly define a product-neutral core whose consumers provide thin adapters. It is therefore Papercusp platform work, not a SideStage product/shared-library plan under D-001, and is explicitly excluded from the SideStage harness migration predicate.\nRelated: P-002, P-003, P-004\n",
