      "contentHash": "df3ffc0e4d97eb6f4ca34099dffe48c8a5e3d2fd7b41e4aa3069fe1d6b54b2c6",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: Sidestage Studio event activation and scheduling UX mockups\nslug: sidestage-studio-event-activation-scheduling-mockups-2026-08-14\nstatus: ready\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n# Sidestage Studio event activation and scheduling UX mockups\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** Complete. Current-state audit, zero-warning interaction model (D-001), four project-bound mockups, validation, and owner delivery are complete; canonical P-001 through P-004 are done.\n\n**Next:** No further work in this design-only plan. Product implementation remains outside scope and behind the Sidestage P-009 release-snapshot gate.\n\n## Background\n\n(Why this plan exists; what problem it addresses.)\n\n## Phase 1 — TODO\n\n(Use plans:add-item to populate. Each item is one line:\nsingle id, status token, free text, optional blocked-by.)\n\n\n## Phase — Discovery and design\n\n- **P-001** `done` Audit the current Studio web experience and source for event activation/start controls importance: high — note: ← WI-39119 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Search the shared UI registry and define the start-now, scheduling, and seller-visibility interaction model blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39122 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Create polished visual mockups grounded in the existing Sidestage interface blocked-by: P-001, P-002 importance: high — note: ← WI-39131 completed (done)\n- **P-004** `done` Validate the mockups and deliver findings with implementation guidance blocked-by: P-003 importance: high — note: ← WI-39134 completed (done)\n- **P-005** `dropped` Audit the current Studio web experience and source for event activation/start controls importance: high — note: Duplicate entries created after multi-ptool output was not surfaced; canonical work remains P-001 through P-004.\n- **P-006** `dropped` Search the shared UI registry and define the start-now, scheduling, and seller-visibility interaction model blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: Duplicate entries created after multi-ptool output was not surfaced; canonical work remains P-001 through P-004.\n- **P-007** `dropped` Create polished visual mockups grounded in the existing Sidestage interface blocked-by: P-001, P-002 importance: high — note: Duplicate entries created after multi-ptool output was not surfaced; canonical work remains P-001 through P-004.\n- **P-008** `dropped` Validate the mockups and deliver findings with implementation guidance blocked-by: P-003 importance: high — note: Duplicate entries created after multi-ptool output was not surfaced; canonical work remains P-001 through P-004.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## Decisions\n\n(Use plans:add-decision to append. Each decision is a third-level\nheading with a date line and a body paragraph.)\n\n### D-001 — Separate event lifecycle activation from publisher media start\nDate: 2026-08-15\nEvent Manager is the authoritative lifecycle surface for a selected event. A draft event exposes a primary `Start now` action and a secondary `Schedule event` action. `Start now` requires a confirmation that names the event and explains that it makes the event buyer-facing/active but does not start the seller's camera or microphone; media start remains the existing Live Console action in Active Event. `Schedule event` uses accessible date, time, and time-zone fields, rejects past times, and saves an explicit scheduled lifecycle state. At the scheduled instant, the server makes the event active for buyers while media remains seller-started in Live Console. Seller-facing Studio surfaces must show the state plus an unambiguous localized date/time and zone: the event list, selected-event header, and Active Event summary show `Scheduled · <date> · <time> <zone>`, with `Edit schedule` and `Start now` available before the scheduled instant. Reuse Sidestage's shipped primary/secondary actions, badge, card, and input patterns; the registry contains no lifecycle or date/time component to reuse.\nRelated: P-002, P-003, P-004\n",
