      "contentHash": "2bf21cade0ca44b10dfb52ee493f8a750c26c7cb5aff5d098685da2a2ca36d2c",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: SideStage Lineup + Run of Show unified redesign mockups\nslug: sidestage-lineup-run-of-show-mockups-2026-08-14\nstatus: ready\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n## Goal\n\nExplore removing the separate Rehearse tab by folding draggable run-of-show authoring into a substantially improved Event Manager Lineup. Produce comparable browser-rendered concepts only; do not alter the production app.\n\n## Constraints\n\nReuse SideStage's existing design language and real event/lineup semantics. Preserve price, inventory, guarded actions, optional time budgets, talking-point notes, and advisory-only live sequencing. Include useful empty/loading/error states and mobile behavior.\n\n## Now\n\nApproved by Avi for direct execution in this session. Registry search found no matching react-tailwind entries, so use shipped SideStage components and tokens as the reuse source.\n\n## Phase — Design exploration\n\n- **P-001** `done` Audit the current Lineup, run-of-show planner, shipped mockups, and SideStage visual tokens; define the shared content model for all concepts. importance: high — note: ← WI-39106 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `todo` Build three interactive browser mockup directions that merge draggable run-of-show planning into a redesigned Lineup, with desktop and mobile behavior. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high\n- **P-003** `todo` Author UI-IR specs for the concepts and run design-phase validation plus anti-pattern lint; correct every blocking issue. blocked-by: P-002 importance: high\n- **P-004** `todo` Run browser visual and interaction QA across the concepts, then present a comparison and recommendation to Avi without modifying production. blocked-by: P-003 importance: high\n\n\n\n\n## Phase — Ad-hoc auction launcher\n\n- **P-005** `done` Search the design registry for SideStage-native panel, action, input, status, product-list, and drawer patterns; capture the current desktop Active Event screen as the visual reference. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39115 completed (done)\n- **P-006** `done` Define three Active Event ad-hoc auction launch concepts—on-deck actions, run-of-show row actions, and a dedicated auction launcher panel—and validate/lint their UI IR. blocked-by: P-005 importance: high — note: ← WI-39121 completed (done)\n- **P-007** `done` Generate one high-fidelity SideStage visual mockup for each validated auction concept using the current Active Event capture as reference. blocked-by: P-006 importance: high — note: ← WI-39123 completed (done)\n- **P-008** `done` Compare live-operation speed, screen density, error prevention, extensibility, and mobile adaptation; present the three auction mockups and a recommendation to Avi. blocked-by: P-007 importance: high — note: ← WI-39130 completed (done)\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D-001 — Ad-hoc auction launch belongs in Active Event\nDate: 2026-08-15\nAvi ruled that seller auction launch is a live-show action, not an Event Manager setup action. Every auction mockup must expose Start auction inside Active Event. Event Manager may retain setup/history, but it cannot be the only launch path.\nRelated: P-005, P-006, P-007, P-008\n",
