          "id": "D-010",
          "title": "Criterion-5 population is the P-009-stamped set, measured mechanically — not a text search; P-009 restored open for the campaign's duration",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nRuling on 3b39b's 15:46Z correction (P-008 criterion 5 = \"zero OPEN critical/major bugs against prod surfaces at cut\").\n\nPOPULATION IS MECHANICAL: the set of kind:bug work-items, severity critical|major, non-terminal, carrying payload.plan_item = {this plan, P-009}. The standing rule (every fix-loop / prod-surface bug gets that stamp AT FILING) is what makes the enumeration complete. An unstamped prod-surface bug is a FILING defect — fix by stamping it, not by widening the claim spec (e1a3a's 15:49Z diagnosis stands: admission blocks were missing stamps, not spec width). Prod-surface = manifests on the deployed prod app, its public API endpoints, its deploy/rollback machinery, or prod data integrity/privacy. Tooling/platform bugs (verdict daemon, launch briefs, plan tooling) and minors are OUT.\n\nPOPULATION AT RULING (re-measured 16:2xZ; 3b39b's two extras EI-20438337753986077 + WI-38835 both closed done ~15:57Z and are OUT):\n- WI-38876 crit (deploy omits schema apply) @61f12\n- WI-38863 crit (PROD checkout credentials absent) @61f12\n- WI-38836 major (probe events visible in prod) @61f12\n- WI-38870 major (compose health-port / verdict trust) @3b39b\n- EI-20444567654586364 major (stats endpoint UNAUTHENTICATED — the surviving half of the 15:57Z fix; being stamped into P-009 now; claimant must FIRST verify at current source whether the EI-20438337753986077 fix already added auth before re-implementing)\n- WI-38827 / WI-38855 / WI-38829 major (judge threshold + latency lane) @55549\n- WI-38872 major (prod npm advisories) — unowned\n\nCLOSE CONDITION: criterion 5 closes only when the stamped set is empty at evaluation AND each close carries deploy-authoritative evidence — per the fleet-wide rule, deploy/deploy.sh's health verdict is NOT evidence until WI-38870 lands.\n\nP-009 GATE: restored to open (was auto-flipped done while stamped bugs were open — EI-20441876140091796 class — blocking admission of critical WI-38876). It stays open for the campaign's duration; no auto-flip to done while any stamped bug is non-terminal.\nRelated: P-008, P-009",
