          "id": "D-012",
          "title": "Empty PROD catalog is a source-selection defect, not missing data: WI-38863 is blocked-by WI-38918, no fixture fabrication, WI-38918 approach authorized, no takeover",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nLeader ruling, 2026-08-14 18:25Z, binding on every P-009 lane.\n\n**1. FINDING (from WI-38918's 18:20Z checkpoint, read directly).** PROD's empty, 11.5s catalog is NOT missing data. `PgCatalogSource` hard-defaults `collection='event-demo-200'` and `runSearch` adds a `c.properties->>'sidestageCollection'` filter, so production selects a curated-demo collection that has **0 rows**, while the real corpus is fully present and unscoped: 1,099,847 product_catalog groups, 1,089,749 active in-stock, Typesense healthy at 1,089,647 docs. Direct prod SQL with `collection=''` returns a six-row page in 117.9ms. The data is there; the source selection hides it.\n\n**2. WI-38863 IS BLOCKED-BY WI-38918, AND ITS PLANNED NEXT STEP IS VACATED.** WI-38863's checkpoint reads \"0 catalog items… checkout cannot start from current data\" with NEXT = \"seed/create test product+event\". That is the SAME defect seen from the buyer lane, and seeding is now prohibited on this plan: it violates WI-38835 (no fixture fabrication) and would prove PROD checkout against fabricated rows — a FALSE POSITIVE on a release-gating criterion, which is worse than a red. Correct sequence: WI-38918's fix exposes 1.09M real in-stock products, then WI-38863 runs the buyer flow (cart → live rates → Square sandbox → paid → orders.byBuyer) against REAL catalog rows. cd8ae's browser/session groundwork stands and is not wasted.\n\n**3. WI-38918'S APPROACH + EXECUTION ROUTE ARE AUTHORIZED** under leader authority (owner's standing AUTO grant on this campaign) — the holder recorded \"no code edit until owner approves approach + execution route\", and that approval is hereby given so the lane does not idle: pass `collection=''` for NODE_ENV=production and `EVENT_DEMO_COLLECTION` otherwise; add source-selection tests proving production/durable PG selects the unscoped real corpus AND development stays curated; add a release positive-control guard (>=6 non-demo in-stock rows + a positive Scout result). Route: the holder implements it himself, in the canonical staging tree. WI-38835 is preserved — fabricate nothing. Deploy remains bound by D-011: only 61f12 invokes SideStage deploy/rollback.\n\n**4. WI-38918 IS NOT AVAILABLE FOR TAKEOVER.** Its holder su-d21f3362 is LIVE (active 8s before this ruling) and mid a DELIBERATE carry-respawn — declared intent: \"Resume WI-38918 only after deterministic carry-respawn; reconcile claim, checkpoint\". A respawning agent reads as claimless and fleetless, which is why leader-brief withheld him and why the item looks unowned; that appearance is an artifact of the respawn window, not an abandonment. His 18:20Z checkpoint already carries the complete root cause, the writer/source proof, the DB counts and the fix design — a takeover discards ~40 minutes of forensics and re-runs them. All peers STAND DOWN on WI-38918. If he has not resumed by 18:45Z, escalate to me; reassignment is the leader's call, not a peer's.\n\n**Generalisation for this fleet:** an empty result from a filtered source is a claim about the FILTER until you have counted the unfiltered rows. Both lanes independently read \"0 items\" as \"no data\" and were both about to act on it — one by seeding fakes, one by taking over.\nRelated: P-009",
