          "id": "D-019",
          "title": "SideStage bridge publication requires a Pot-attested integrator signer; never bypass wrong-device rejection",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nEvidence from the 2026-08-14 21:04 EDT git-sync writer: own_head_publish advanced cleanly to e49a5428e4129dc4922541eb58d8c7baa2dcb88e, but integrator_status skipped with self_device_not_attested because local signer device XPAsvso1qEKb… is not among SideStage's attested devices. worktree_bridge recorded 16 consecutive consumed=1 / accepted=0 ticks and rejected the current advance as wrong-device; canonical GitHub origin/staging therefore remained 46db8556738ed345415e3ffc4a59927e2a7ca621. RULING: repair the signer through the existing Pot membership/device-attestation surface; do not direct-push or otherwise route around the bridge's device guard. Then fire the existing git-sync flow and require, in order, canonical/origin advancement, fresh-clone resolution of the corrected head, the full D-018 SSE/API/web/Node20 image + /healthz matrix, a changed public SHA, and populated-catalog positive control before deployment or P-005/WI-38945 closure.\nRelated: P-005",
