          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nWI-38968 currently proves a post-restart writer contradiction: the new self_device_not_attested guard executed on one Papercusp git-sync tick, while another writer/path subsequently signed four advances from the same unadmitted XPAs… device. Its current broadcast prohibits manual git-sync:run for Papercusp until 70ba41c9 is deployed, but the evidence does not yet establish whether that stale/concurrent writer is Papercusp-local or shared with SideStage. TEMPORARY RULING: WI-38945 may continue the existing SideStage Pot device-attestation repair and read-only proof preparation, but must not manually fire SideStage git-sync until the live WI-38968 owner answers the scope and exact safe next verb. D-019 and the no-deploy/no-close proof chain remain fully operative. This hold narrows only the manual git-sync invocation and must be superseded immediately when the writer owner supplies verified scope.\nRelated: P-005",
