          "title": "D-020 resolved: SideStage manual git-sync is safe only after exact actor attestation and a clean scheduled tick",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nWI-38968 owner verified the temporary manual-run prohibition is scoped to installSlug=papercusp, including an omitted/default slug that resolves to Papercusp; it is not a blanket ban on every bridged Pot. The exact failure predicate is runtime resolveUsageActor.devicePubkey absent from listHiveMembersForLocalPot(...).deviceAttestations, causing old manual code to sign and receivers to reject wrong-device. SUPERSEDES D-020: WI-38945 may release its temporary hold only after (1) the exact SideStage runtime actor key is present in the resolved SideStage Pot attestation set and (2) a scheduled SideStage tick no longer records self_device_not_attested or wrong-device. Only then may it call git-sync:run with the explicit argument installSlug:'sidestage'—never omit/default the slug. If membership equality or the clean scheduled tick is not proven, wait for the scheduled tick or for 70ba41c9 to reach the live release operator; do not use the old manual plane. Current writer loading at the ruling: 70ba41c9 is on origin/staging and loaded by bg-host source, but not in main/live :3070; checkpoint candidate 6bcdb023 is still running. D-019's no-bypass and full fresh-clone/runtime/public proof chain remain mandatory.\nRelated: P-005",
